# The markup IR parser

This parses the output of noweb's `markup` pipeline — the IR lit consumes instead
of driving `noweave`. It is verified against noweb 2.13 (SPEC.md §4.2): `markup`
lives in `lib/noweb`, an empty text line arrives with a trailing space, and a fatal
error shows up both as a nonzero exit and an `@fatal` event.

The module is the event type, a line parser, and the `markup` runner that ties them
together.
